Package: crossRanger
Type: Package
Title: Cross-Application of Ranger Models Using Microbiome Data
Version: 0.2.0
Author: Shi Huang
Maintainer: Shi Huang <shihuang047@gmail.com>
Description: Builds multiple random forest models with 'ranger' according to metadata for a given
    dataset or for multiple datasets, using out-of-bag estimation, stratified k-fold, group k-fold or
    leave-one-group-out cross-validation; applies the models to each other and performs
    leave-one-dataset-out validation; identifies biomarkers by recursive feature elimination
    and univariate statistical tests; and visualizes the results and generates R Markdown reports.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://github.com/HuangShiLab/crossRanger
BugReports: https://github.com/HuangShiLab/crossRanger/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports:
  ranger, stats, utils, graphics, parallel, foreach, doParallel, compositions, grDevices, PRROC, rlang, gtools,
  Matrix, ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0), pROC, caret, corrplot, gridExtra, plyr, reshape2, viridis
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown, grid
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
